1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,899
ACR brings compute benchmarks, billing evidence,

2
00:00:03,749 --> 00:00:06,802
and on-chain infrastructure into one product.

3
00:00:07,452 --> 00:00:10,284
Let’s check a bill in the chat: forty-seven cents

4
00:00:10,134 --> 00:00:13,442
for twenty-three thousand inference tokens. Aomi

5
00:00:13,292 --> 00:00:16,693
calls ACR’s bill checker and rate tool. You

6
00:00:16,543 --> 00:00:19,235
can inspect the actual calls as they run, then

7
00:00:19,085 --> 00:00:20,513
read the recommendation.

8
00:00:27,452 --> 00:00:29,970
Open the trace. The bill checker receives the

9
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:33,221
total amount and twenty-three units of one thousand

10
00:00:33,071 --> 00:00:36,298
tokens. Its response includes five public price

11
00:00:36,148 --> 00:00:39,374
references and the age of the evidence. The separate

12
00:00:39,224 --> 00:00:42,323
rate call returns the oracle address and index

13
00:00:42,173 --> 00:00:42,973
freshness.

14
00:00:43,623 --> 00:00:46,652
Aomi recommends review because this example is

15
00:00:46,502 --> 00:00:50,251
about fifty-one times the returned market benchmark.

16
00:00:50,101 --> 00:00:53,467
It also says the price evidence is nearly thirteen

17
00:00:53,317 --> 00:00:56,579
days old. Different models and billing terms may

18
00:00:56,429 --> 00:00:59,087
not be comparable. The index is separate from

19
00:00:58,937 --> 00:01:01,652
market pricing, and no payment has been made.

20
00:01:08,442 --> 00:01:11,119
This is more than an API integration.

21
00:01:11,159 --> 00:01:14,648
ACR has an on-chain oracle, attestations,

22
00:01:14,688 --> 00:01:16,780
and settlement infrastructure.

23
00:01:16,871 --> 00:01:18,874
Aomi connects protocol-specific

24
00:01:18,914 --> 00:01:20,976
knowledge and off-chain records

25
00:01:21,016 --> 00:01:25,138
to a harness that can prepare reviewed contract actions.

26
00:01:25,589 --> 00:01:26,652
For treasury payments,

27
00:01:26,692 --> 00:01:29,241
the recorded bill determines the recipient,

28
00:01:29,281 --> 00:01:32,004
amount, category, and decision hash.

29
00:01:32,044 --> 00:01:35,034
Aomi stages spendAsOwner, simulates it,

30
00:01:35,074 --> 00:01:37,275
and requests owner authorization.

31
00:01:37,315 --> 00:01:40,015
The guard restricts chain, contract, and function;

32
00:01:40,055 --> 00:01:42,209
PolicyWallet enforces ownership,

33
00:01:42,249 --> 00:01:45,072
budget, and replay protection.

34
00:01:45,522 --> 00:01:49,313
After payment, ACR verifies the successful receipt and

35
00:01:49,353 --> 00:01:52,413
matching event before reconciling the original bill.

36
00:01:52,453 --> 00:01:54,991
That closes the loop: off-chain evidence,

37
00:01:55,031 --> 00:01:56,837
authorized on-chain action,

38
00:01:56,877 --> 00:01:59,850
and a business record that knows what settled.

39
00:02:00,301 --> 00:02:03,593
That is the foundation for one-shotting a protocol app.

40
00:02:03,633 --> 00:02:05,927
Describe the workflow, connect the infrastructure,

41
00:02:05,967 --> 00:02:08,736
and define the contract actions and guards.

42
00:02:08,776 --> 00:02:11,477
Aomi supplies the agent runtime and frontend

43
00:02:11,517 --> 00:02:14,676
component around those protocol-specific pieces.

44
00:02:15,126 --> 00:02:17,315
The frontend integration is shipped.

45
00:02:17,355 --> 00:02:19,753
The treasury workflow is implemented,

46
00:02:19,793 --> 00:02:22,249
with production payment acceptance still pending.

47
00:02:22,289 --> 00:02:24,618
The value is one agent that connects

48
00:02:24,658 --> 00:02:27,875
understanding the protocol with acting on it.
